{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310736,"nonce":"o/tMNszcghelJ1Fbi0SGBDJm8L4=","title":"Auto-deriving Send/Sync/Clone recursed forever on a cyclic type graph, overflowing the compiler stack on any mutually referential classes","message":"**FIXED 2026-08-21.** `rayzor run` on `compiler/benchmarks/src/deltablue.hx`\naborted with `fatal runtime error: stack overflow` on BOTH tiers. The message is\nRUST's — the COMPILER process overflowed, not the compiled program. That\ndistinction is the whole diagnosis; treat \"stack overflow\" from a rayzor run as\na compiler bug until shown otherwise.\n\n**Finding it:** a stack overflow aborts with no backtrace, but macOS writes\n`~/Library/Logs/DiagnosticReports/rayzor-*.ips`. Parse the JSON body (skip the\nfirst header line), take the `triggered` thread's frames, and count repeats —\nthe recursion names itself:\n\n```\n7x TraitChecker::implements_trait\n6x TraitChecker::class_implements_trait\n```\n\n**Cause:** `class_implements_trait` auto-derives by asking the same question of\nEVERY field's type (`auto_derive_send` -\u003e `is_send(field.field_type)` -\u003e\n`implements_trait` -\u003e ...). A cycle in the type graph therefore asks the\nquestion of the class currently being answered. deltablue is a constraint\nsolver: `Variable.constraints: Array\u003cConstraint\u003e` and `Constraint.myOutput:\nVariable`. Nothing tracked in-progress questions.\n\n**Fix:** `in_progress: RefCell\u003cHashSet\u003c(SymbolId, DerivedTrait)\u003e\u003e` on\n`TraitChecker`; a question already on the stack answers `true` and lets the\nother fields decide. That is the GREATEST fixed point and is what Rust does for\nauto traits — a genuinely non-Send leaf anywhere still returns false, so it does\nnot weaken the check.\n\n**Verified by cross-implementation, not just by terminating:** rayzor prints\n`total: 14065400` and HashLink/C on the portable `BMDeltaBlueCode.hx` prints\n`total: 14065400`. Same answer from an independent implementation.\n\n**This was invisible because deltablue is not in the Haxe suite** — it lives in\n`compiler/benchmarks/`, which only `benchmark_runner` touches, and its rayzor\nrows had simply been absent from the results JSON rather than reported as\nfailures.\n\nRelated: [[bugs_silent_test_failures_2026_08_12]],\n[[reference_hashlink_bench_arm64_limits]].\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_trait_autoderive_infinite_recursion` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}